{
    "background_story": "Kaizen, a gentle sea turtle, had a remarkable experience when he was just a hatchling. As he emerged from his egg, he was covered in a sticky, black substance called meconium. This tar-like coating not only protected him from predators but also provided essential nutrients during his first few days of life. As he made his way to the ocean, Kaizen shed this vital layer, revealing his vibrant, green shell beneath. The memory of his meconium-covered beginning stayed with him as a reminder of the incredible journey he had undertaken. As he grew, Kaizen became a symbol of resilience and adaptation, inspiring other sea creatures with his remarkable transformation from vulnerable hatchling to majestic sea turtle.",
